# `when` has one place, after the result, and one shape, an unsigned integer
# literal, `true` or `false` (panel 177's item 6), and every misplacement is
# its line's ONLY diagnostic. Until 2026-09-25 a clause with no `->` and a
# clause on a parameter were generic member and `)` errors that named no rule
# (findings 2 and 5 of the sitting's landing), a refused literal was left
# standing and reported a second time as a member the group could not read
# (finding 3), and a `|` dangling at the end of a releaser set was reported on
# the NEXT declaration's line, since a trailing bar continues the line
# (finding 4). The bar is last here because it does continue the line: what
# follows it is read as the set's next name.
extern "success-clause-placement.h"
    record Ob tag ob
    function ob_put(o: Ob consumes) when 0  #~ success_needs_result
    function ob_neg(o: Ob consumes) -> i32 when -1  #~ expected_success_value
    function ob_chr(o: Ob consumes) -> i32 when 'a'  #~ expected_success_value
    function ob_flt(o: Ob consumes) -> i32 when 1.0  #~ expected_success_value
    function ob_nam(o: Ob consumes) -> i32 when SQLITE_OK  #~ expected_success_value
    function ob_par(o: Ob consumes when 0) -> i32  #~ success_on_parameter
    function ob_new() -> Ob acquires ob_put |  #~ expected_releaser

function main()
    print(0)
